// ============================================================================
//  INTRABAR FILL AMBIGUITY - STATED HONESTLY, ONCE
//
//  On any bar whose range contains BOTH the live stop and the live target, the
//  order in which they were touched is NOT in the OHLC data. TradingView's
//  broker emulator does not know it either: it GUESSES from the bar's open, on
//  the assumption that price travelled open -> nearest extreme -> other
//  extreme. That guess is systematically FLATTERING here, because a
//  mean-reversion entry usually opens nearer its target than its stop, so the
//  emulator tends to resolve the ambiguous bar as a win.
//
//  SECTION 15's virtual ledger assumes the OPPOSITE - STOP FIRST - on every
//  such bar. The two will therefore disagree on exactly the bars that matter
//  most, and the size of that disagreement is the honest measure of how much of
//  the result is path assumption rather than edge. The report row "Ambiguous
//  bars: n% of bars in trade" makes it visible: at 1% the question is moot, at
//  15% the equity curve is mostly a coin flip.
//
//  MITIGATIONS, and what each actually costs:
//    * BAR MAGNIFIER - resolves the path from real lower-timeframe data. It is
//      the only true fix. It is a PAID feature (Premium and above) and this
//      account does not have it, so it is unavailable here.
//    * fill_orders_on_standard_ohlc = true in the strategy() call - forces fills
//      to be computed from standard OHLC even on a non-standard chart. It does
//      NOT resolve intrabar order; it only stops Heikin-Ashi / Renko prices from
//      manufacturing fills at prices that never traded. Worth setting anyway.
//    * calc_on_every_tick = true - changes nothing on historical bars, which is
//      where the entire backtest lives. It is NOT a mitigation, despite being
//      widely cited as one.
//    * Widening TP1 so it and the stop cannot share a bar - shrinks the
//      ambiguity by shrinking the strategy. That is a real cost, not a free fix.
//
//  RECOMMENDED HONEST DEFAULT: leave the emulator's behaviour as-is, keep
//  fill_orders_on_standard_ohlc = true, read the ambiguous-bar share on every
//  run, and treat SECTION 15's stop-first ledger as the LOWER bound and the
//  Strategy Tester as the UPPER bound. Quote the pair. Never quote the upper
//  bound alone.
// ============================================================================
// ========================= END SECTION 18 ===================================
